*
* =====================================================================
*  MESH SENSITIVITY / CONVERGENCE STUDY - FINE MESH MODEL
*  Derived from current/staad/Underground_Structure_WITH_LOADS_worked_example (4).STD
*  (the reconciled M1 model = the MEDIUM/reference mesh of this study).
*  Geometry, thicknesses, materials, supports, loads, load cases and
*  combinations are IDENTICAL to the reference model.  ONLY the plate
*  mesh density differs.  See MESH_SENSITIVITY_STUDY.md for the full
*  methodology, panel-by-panel derivation and convergence results.
*
*  MESH: nominal element edge X 0.2625-0.5 m, Z 0.2625-0.35 m (horizontal panels);
*  wall row height Y 0.3292 m.  Average in-plane element size approx.
*  0.334 (horiz) / 0.3292 (vert) m.
*  Joints: 4500   Plate elements: 4552
*  Grid : X 61 stations, Z 19 stations, Y 13 stations
*
*  MESHING METHOD - structured grid, identical to the reference model's
*  own convention (see its header note on joint numbering).  Coarsening
*  and refinement are done on the reference grid lines themselves: FINE
*  inserts one new grid line at the exact midpoint of every reference
*  interval (uniform h/2 refinement, so it reproduces the reference
*  geometry exactly).  COARSE removes alternating reference grid lines
*  while always keeping the lines that define the outer box, the W5/
*  W6/W7 centrelines and every opening edge (stair shaft, both escape
*  shafts), so wall centrelines, thicknesses and opening geometry are
*  pixel-for-pixel identical in all three models.  Where an opening or
*  a wall centreline forces an odd number of reference intervals in a
*  bay, one element in that bay is left un-doubled - a local, documented
*  mesh-size variation, not an error (flagged again in the study report).
*
*  NUMBERING (same scheme as the reference model, resized to this grid):
*  n = (k-1)*1159 + (i-1)*19 + j   i = X index 1..61,
*  j = Z index 1..19, k = Y index 1..13.
* =====================================================================
*
*  REV MS2 (11 Sep 2026, master Part H.26) - INPUT-FILE CORRECTIONS ONLY.  No geometry, thickness,
*  material, support, load magnitude or combination was changed; the analysis
*  model is identical to MS1.  LOAD 10 now precedes LOAD 11 so the primary load
*  case numbers ascend 1..11 (case numbers, factors and all five combinations
*  unchanged), and the LOAD 11 title and JOB CLIENT line now fit INPUT WIDTH 79.
*
